"h":500,"by":"Alexbrn","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stornoway_Black_Pudding.jpg"}},"ingredient/pickled-bean-curd":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pickled-bean-curd","n":"Pickled bean curd","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Fermented tofu (also called fermented bean curd, white bean-curd cheese, tofu cheese, soy cheese, preserved tofu or sufu) is a Chinese  condiment consisting of a form of processed, preserved  tofu used in East Asian cuisine; typical ingredients are soybeans, salt, rice wine and sesame oil or vinegar."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pickled-bean-curd"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pickled_bean_curd"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["Boat noodles","dish/boat-noodles"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bean sprouts","ingredient/bean-sprouts"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Dark soy sauce","ingredient/dark-soy-sauce"],["Fermented bean curd","ingredient/fermented-bean-curd"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Morning glory","ingredient/morning-glory"],["Paprika","ingredient/paprika"],["Parsley","ingredient/parsley"],["Pig blood","ingredient/pig-blood"],["Radish","ingredient/radish"],["Rice noodles","ingredient/rice-noodles"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/db/Fermentedchilibeancurd.jpg/500px-Fermentedchilibeancurd.jpg","w":500,"h":272,"by":"Hmm...","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fermentedchilibeancurd.jpg"}},"dish/rice-and-beans":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/rice-and-beans","n":"Rice and beans","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Latin American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Rice and beans, or beans and rice, is a category of dishes from many cultures around the world where the staple foods of rice and beans are combined in some manner. The grain and legume combination provides several important nutrients and many calories, and both foods are widely available. The beans are usually seasoned, while the rice may be plain or seasoned. If the beans do not top the rice, the two components may be mixed together, separated on the plate, or served separately."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-rice-and-beans"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rice_and_beans"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Latin American cuisine","cuisine/latin-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Beans","ingredient/beans"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"More from Latin American cuisine","links":[["Bollo","dish/bollo"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Frijoles negros","dish/frijoles-negros"],["Quince cheese","dish/quince-cheese"],["Tamale","dish/tamale"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/ca/Rice_and_Beans.jpg/500px-Rice_and_Beans.jpg","w":500,"h":224,"by":"Lorena Galicia","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rice_and_Beans.jpg"}},"dish/saheena":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/saheena","n":"Saheena","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Trinidad and Tobago cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Saheena (also spelled sahina or sahiena, ) is a street food and snack in the cuisine of Trinidad and Tobago."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-saheena"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saheena"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Trinidad and Tobago cuisine","cuisine/trinidad-and-tobago-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Spinach","ingredient/spinach"],["Split pea","ingredient/split-pea"],["Taro","ingredient/taro"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Cooking with Ria","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cookingwithria.com","note":"Trinidadian home recipes from Ria Mathura.","url":"https://cookingwithria.com/about","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Trini Gourmet","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"trinigourmet.com","note":"Long-running Trinidad and Tobago food blog with local recipes.","url":"https://trinigourmet.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/19/FOOD_Saheena_1.jpg/500px-FOOD_Saheena_1.jpg","w":500,"h":650,"by":"Grueslayer","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FOOD_Saheena_1.jpg"}},"dish/wahe":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/wahe","n":"Wähe","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Swiss cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Wähe (which derives from the dialect in the regions of Basel, Zurich, Baden and Alsace) is a baked dish typical of Swiss and Alemannic (German) cuisine. A wähe consists of a casing (typically made of shortcrust pastry, but sometimes yeast dough or puff pastry) and a topping of a custard enveloping either fruit, vegetables or cheese. The custard and fruits or vegetables are baked together. The preparation is thus very similar to that of the French quiche or tarte."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-wahe"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W%C3%A4he"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Custard","ingredient/custard"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Helvetic Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"helvetickitchen.com","note":"Andie Pilot's blog of Swiss home cooking and baking, with notes on Swiss cookbooks.","url":"https://www.helvetickitchen.com/recipes/retrospective","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Cuisine Helvetica","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cuisinehelvetica.com","note":"Heddi Nieuwsma's Swiss recipes and food culture from her life in Switzerland.","url":"https://cuisinehelvetica.com/swiss-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Swiss cuisine","links":[["Älplermagronen","dish/alplermagronen"],["Basler Läckerli","dish/basler-lackerli"],["Birnbrot","dish/birnbrot"],["Bündnerfleisch","dish/bundnerfleisch"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Carac (pastry)","dish/carac-pastry"],["Cervelat","dish/cervelat"],["Cholera (food)","dish/cholera-food"],["Egg puffs and soup pearls","dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls"],["Landjäger","dish/landjager"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Raclette","dish/raclette"],["Riz Casimir","dish/riz-casimir"],["Schenkele","dish/schenkele"],["Spätzle","dish/spatzle"],["Swiss sausages and cured meats","dish/swiss-sausages-and-cured-meats"],["Zopf","dish/zopf"],["Zuger Kirschtorte","dish/zuger-kirschtorte"],["Zürcher Geschnetzeltes","dish/zurcher-geschnetzeltes"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9a/K%C3%A4sd%C3%B6nnala_Rad.jpg/500px-K%C3%A4sd%C3%B6nnala_Rad.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Reinhard Müller","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%A4sd%C3%B6nnala_Rad.jpg"}}}